# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the CPU, memory, and GPU resources for a managed workflow, and define sizes that match the size of the problem."
msgstr "Piliin ang mga resource ng CPU, memory, at GPU para sa isang managed workflow, at tukuyin ang mga size na tumutugma sa laki ng problema."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a compute profile"
msgstr "Pumili ng compute profile"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a compute profile {#choose-a-compute-profile}"
msgstr "Pumili ng compute profile {#choose-a-compute-profile}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Managed workflows run on compute profiles. A compute profile is a fixed combination of vCPUs, memory, and GPUs, similar to the resources that you request from an HPC scheduler. When you upload a workflow, you map its sizes, such as `S` and `M`, to profiles, and each run picks one of those sizes. The job then runs on its own node with that profile, and keeps the profile until the job ends.\n"
msgstr "Tumatakbo ang mga managed workflow sa mga compute profile. Ang compute profile ay isang nakatakdang kombinasyon ng mga vCPU, memory, at GPU, katulad ng mga resource na hinihiling mo mula sa isang HPC scheduler. Kapag nag-upload ka ng workflow, imamapa mo ang mga size nito, gaya ng `S` at `M`, sa mga profile, at pipili ang bawat run ng isa sa mga size na iyon. Tatakbo ang job sa sarili nitong node gamit ang profile na iyon, at pinapanatili nito ang profile hanggang matapos ang job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Profile | vCPUs | Memory (GB) | GPUs |\n"
"| - | - | - | - |\n"
"| `8x32` | 8 | 32 | None |\n"
"| `16x128` | 16 | 128 | None |\n"
"| `48x768` | 48 | 768 | None |\n"
"| `128x1500` | 128 | 1500 | None |\n"
"| `24x120x1l40s` | 24 | 120 | 1 L40S |\n"
"| `20x320x2a100` | 20 | 320 | 2 A100 |\n"
"| `80x1200x8a100` | 80 | 1200 | 8 A100 |\n"
"| `160x1792x8h100` | 160 | 1792 | 8 H100 |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Profile | Mga vCPU | Memory (GB) | Mga GPU |\n"
"| - | - | - | - |\n"
"| `8x32` | 8 | 32 | Wala |\n"
"| `16x128` | 16 | 128 | Wala |\n"
"| `48x768` | 48 | 768 | Wala |\n"
"| `128x1500` | 128 | 1500 | Wala |\n"
"| `24x120x1l40s` | 24 | 120 | 1 L40S |\n"
"| `20x320x2a100` | 20 | 320 | 2 A100 |\n"
"| `80x1200x8a100` | 80 | 1200 | 8 A100 |\n"
"| `160x1792x8h100` | 160 | 1792 | 8 H100 |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A profile ID has the form `{cpu}x{memory}`, with memory in GB, or `{cpu}x{memory}x{count}{gpu}` for a profile with GPUs. For example, `24x120x1l40s` has 24 vCPUs, 120 GB of memory, and one NVIDIA L40S GPU.\n"
msgstr "Ang profile ID ay may anyong `{cpu}x{memory}`, na ang memory ay nasa GB, o `{cpu}x{memory}x{count}{gpu}` para sa profile na may mga GPU. Halimbawa, ang `24x120x1l40s` ay may 24 na vCPU, 120 GB ng memory, at isang NVIDIA L40S GPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check available profiles {#check-available-profiles}"
msgstr "Tingnan ang mga available na profile {#check-available-profiles}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see which profiles are available, call `compute_profiles()`:\n"
msgstr "Para makita kung aling mga profile ang available, tawagin ang `compute_profiles()`:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Look up a profile by its resources {#look-up-a-profile-by-its-resources}"
msgstr "Maghanap ng profile ayon sa mga resource nito {#look-up-a-profile-by-its-resources}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of typing a profile ID, you can describe the resources that your workflow needs with `compute_profile()`, and use the result as a value in `sizes_map`. Pass `cpu` and `memory` in GB, and pass `gpu` for a GPU profile:\n"
msgstr "Sa halip na mag-type ng profile ID, maaari mong ilarawan ang mga resource na kailangan ng workflow mo gamit ang `compute_profile()`, at gamitin ang resulta bilang value sa `sizes_map`. Ipasa ang `cpu` at `memory` sa GB, at ipasa ang `gpu` para sa GPU profile:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `sizes_map` accepts profile IDs and the profiles that `compute_profile()` returns, and you can mix both in one map. To check a profile ID before you upload, pass it to `compute_profile()`, for example `client.compute_profile(\"16x128\")`. If no profile matches, the error lists the available profiles.\n"
msgstr "Tumatanggap ang `sizes_map` ng mga profile ID at ng mga profile na ibinabalik ng `compute_profile()`, at maaari mong paghaluin ang dalawa sa iisang map. Para suriin ang isang profile ID bago mag-upload, ipasa ito sa `compute_profile()`, halimbawa `client.compute_profile(\"16x128\")`. Kung walang profile na tumutugma, inililista ng error ang mga available na profile.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_profiles()` returns a list, so you can also filter it yourself. For example, the following code finds the GPU profiles:\n"
msgstr "Ang `compute_profiles()` ay nagbabalik ng list, kaya maaari mo rin itong i-filter nang mag-isa. Halimbawa, hinahanap ng sumusunod na code ang mga GPU profile:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set a default compute profile for your workflow {#set-a-default-compute-profile-for-your-workflow}"
msgstr "Magtakda ng default na compute profile para sa workflow mo {#set-a-default-compute-profile-for-your-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Most workflows start with one size. Map it to a profile with `sizes_map`, and make it the default with `default_size`, when you upload the workflow:\n"
msgstr "Karamihan ng mga workflow ay nagsisimula sa isang size. Imapa ito sa isang profile gamit ang `sizes_map`, at gawin itong default gamit ang `default_size`, kapag ina-upload ang workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every run of the workflow uses this profile, so you do not need to pass a size when you run it:\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng bawat run ng workflow ang profile na ito, kaya hindi mo kailangang magpasa ng size kapag pinatakbo mo ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: match sizes to problem sizes {#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes}"
msgstr "Best practice: itugma ang mga size sa laki ng problema {#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A workflow solves specific problems, and it might require different compute profiles as the problems increase in scale and complexity. With a `sizes_map` for each workflow, you can do the following:\n"
msgstr "Ang isang workflow ay lumulutas ng mga partikular na problema, at maaaring mangailangan ito ng iba't ibang compute profile habang lumalaki ang sukat at pagiging kumplikado ng mga problema. Sa isang `sizes_map` para sa bawat workflow, magagawa mo ang mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Give large problems enough compute resources to run to completion.\n"
msgstr "Bigyan ang malalaking problema ng sapat na compute resource para makumpleto ang pagtakbo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prevent small problems from using a larger node than they need.\n"
msgstr "Pigilan ang maliliit na problema na gumamit ng mas malaking node kaysa sa kailangan nila.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can base the sizes on the factors that determine your workflow's memory and CPU use, such as the subspace size, the number of batches, or the number of qubits.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mong ibatay ang mga size sa mga salik na tumutukoy sa paggamit ng memory at CPU ng workflow mo, gaya ng laki ng subspace, bilang ng mga batch, o bilang ng mga qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the sizes {#define-the-sizes}"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang mga size {#define-the-sizes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can map up to four sizes, for small (`S`), medium (`M`), large (`L`), and extra-large (`XL`) problems. For example, the following code defines a workflow with three sizes:\n"
msgstr "Maaari kang magmapa ng hanggang apat na size, para sa maliliit (`S`), katamtaman (`M`), malalaki (`L`), at napakalalaking (`XL`) problema. Halimbawa, nagtatakda ang sumusunod na code ng workflow na may tatlong size:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Size rules {#size-rules}"
msgstr "Mga patakaran sa size {#size-rules}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Size labels must be `S`, `M`, `L`, or `XL`, so a workflow can define up to four sizes. A managed workflow matches labels in uppercase or lowercase, and stores them in uppercase. Two sizes can map to the same profile.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga size label ay dapat na `S`, `M`, `L`, o `XL`, kaya ang isang workflow ay maaaring magtakda ng hanggang apat na size. Tinutugma ng managed workflow ang mga label sa uppercase o lowercase, at iniimbak ang mga ito sa uppercase. Maaaring mapa ang dalawang size sa iisang profile.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A workflow rejects the first upload in the following cases:\n"
msgstr "Tinatanggihan ng workflow ang unang upload sa mga sumusunod na kaso:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A label is not `S`, `M`, `L`, or `XL`.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang label ay hindi `S`, `M`, `L`, o `XL`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You set `sizes_map` without `default_size`, or `default_size` without `sizes_map`.\n"
msgstr "Itinakda mo ang `sizes_map` nang walang `default_size`, o ang `default_size` nang walang `sizes_map`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`default_size` is not one of the labels in `sizes_map`.\n"
msgstr "Ang `default_size` ay hindi isa sa mga label sa `sizes_map`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A value in `sizes_map` is not an available compute profile.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang value sa `sizes_map` ay hindi available na compute profile.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change sizes on re-upload {#change-sizes-on-re-upload}"
msgstr "Baguhin ang mga size sa muling pag-upload {#change-sizes-on-re-upload}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you upload the workflow again with the same `title`, the managed workflow handles the sizes as follows:\n"
msgstr "Kapag muli mong in-upload ang workflow gamit ang parehong `title`, ganito hinahawakan ng managed workflow ang mga size:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you set `sizes_map`, the new sizes replace all of the stored sizes.\n"
msgstr "Kung itinakda mo ang `sizes_map`, pinapalitan ng mga bagong size ang lahat ng naka-store na size.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you omit `sizes_map`, the workflow keeps the stored sizes and the default.\n"
msgstr "Kung hindi mo itinakda ang `sizes_map`, pinapanatili ng workflow ang mga naka-store na size at ang default.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To change only the default, set `default_size` without `sizes_map`. The value of `default_size` must be one of the stored sizes.\n"
msgstr "Para baguhin lang ang default, itakda ang `default_size` nang walang `sizes_map`. Ang value ng `default_size` ay dapat isa sa mga naka-store na size.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set `default_size` every time that you set `sizes_map`. A re-upload does not require `default_size`. If the new sizes do not include the old default, the workflow has no default, and every run without `function_size` fails.\n"
msgstr "Itakda ang `default_size` tuwing itinatakda mo ang `sizes_map`. Hindi nangangailangan ng `default_size` ang muling pag-upload. Kung hindi kasama sa mga bagong size ang dating default, walang default ang workflow, at pumapalya ang bawat run na walang `function_size`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a size for each run {#choose-a-size-for-each-run}"
msgstr "Pumili ng size para sa bawat run {#choose-a-size-for-each-run}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass `function_size` to `run()` to choose one of the workflow's sizes for that job. If you omit it, the job uses the workflow's default size:\n"
msgstr "Ipasa ang `function_size` sa `run()` para pumili ng isa sa mga size ng workflow para sa job na iyon. Kung hindi mo ito ipapasa, gagamitin ng job ang default na size ng workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`sizes()` and `get_default_size()` return the sizes that were stored when you loaded the workflow. To see sizes that changed after you loaded the workflow, load it again.\n"
msgstr "Ibinabalik ng `sizes()` at `get_default_size()` ang mga size na naka-store noong nilo-load mo ang workflow. Para makita ang mga size na nagbago pagkatapos mong i-load ang workflow, i-load itong muli.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To read the size and compute profile of the job, call `get_function_size()` and `get_compute_profile()` in your workflow code:\n"
msgstr "Para basahin ang size at compute profile ng job, tawagin ang `get_function_size()` at `get_compute_profile()` sa code ng workflow mo:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot sizes {#troubleshoot-sizes}"
msgstr "Mag-troubleshoot ng mga size {#troubleshoot-sizes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| The upload fails with `Invalid size '...'. Valid sizes are: S, M, L, XL.` | A label in `sizes_map` is not one of the four supported labels. |\n"
"| The upload fails with `Unknown compute profile '...' for size '...'.` | A value in `sizes_map` is not an available profile. Check the ID with `compute_profiles()`, or use `compute_profile()` to look it up. |\n"
"| `compute_profile()` fails with `No compute profile matches ...` | No profile has exactly those resources. For a GPU profile, also pass `gpu`. Pick a profile from the list in the error. |\n"
"| The upload fails with `'default_size' is required when 'sizes' is provided.` | The first upload sets `sizes_map` without `default_size`. |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `Unknown function size '...' for this function. Available sizes: ...` | The workflow does not define the size that you passed to `function_size`. |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `This function has no size.` | A re-upload replaced the sizes and removed the default. Upload again with `default_size`, or pass `function_size`. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Sanhi |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang upload na may `Invalid size '...'. Valid sizes are: S, M, L, XL.` | Ang isang label sa `sizes_map` ay hindi isa sa apat na sinusuportahang label. |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang upload na may `Unknown compute profile '...' for size '...'.` | Ang isang value sa `sizes_map` ay hindi available na profile. Suriin ang ID gamit ang `compute_profiles()`, o gamitin ang `compute_profile()` para hanapin ito. |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang `compute_profile()` na may `No compute profile matches ...` | Walang profile na may eksaktong mga resource na iyon. Para sa GPU profile, ipasa rin ang `gpu`. Pumili ng profile mula sa listahan sa error. |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang upload na may `'default_size' is required when 'sizes' is provided.` | Itinakda ng unang upload ang `sizes_map` nang walang `default_size`. |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang `run()` na may `Unknown function size '...' for this function. Available sizes: ...` | Hindi tinutukoy ng workflow ang size na ipinasa mo sa `function_size`. |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang `run()` na may `This function has no size.` | Pinalitan ng muling pag-upload ang mga size at inalis ang default. Mag-upload muli gamit ang `default_size`, o ipasa ang `function_size`. |\n"
